## Highlights
► Porphyrinic metal-organic framework (MOFs) is designed as nanocarrier and electrochemical probe without adding extra redox media.
► Pt NPs grown on the surface of MOFs could maintain high stability and catalytic activity.
► The synergy between Pt NPs and MOFs enhances the high electrocatalytic activity of Pt@P-MOF(Fe) towards to \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) reduction and increases the electrochemical signal.
► The signal was amplified by triple-helix molecular switch and Exonuclease III.
► The telomerase activity sensor showed good performance.
